The project is named "TerminalSnake".

Set game_over to 0.
Set snake_x to 10.
Set snake_y to 10.
Set food_x to 15.
Set food_y to 15.

Clear the terminal.

Repeat while game_over is 0:
    Note: Draw the game state.
    Clear the terminal.
    Draw terminal box at 0, 0 with width 30 and height 20.
    
    Move cursor to food_x, food_y.
    Print "@" colored "red".
    
    Move cursor to snake_x, snake_y.
    Print "O" colored "green".
    
    Note: Read input non-blocking.
    Wait for key press as input_key.
    
    If input_key is "w":
        Set snake_y to (snake_y - 1).
    If input_key is "s":
        Set snake_y to (snake_y + 1).
    If input_key is "a":
        Set snake_x to (snake_x - 1).
    If input_key is "d":
        Set snake_x to (snake_x + 1).
    If input_key is "q":
        Set game_over to 1.
    
    If (snake_x == food_x) and (snake_y == food_y):
        Set food_x to a random number between 1 and 28.
        Set food_y to a random number between 1 and 18.
    
    Sleep for 100 milliseconds.

Clear the terminal.
Print "Game Over!" colored "red".
